# Date Format — UK Only (`DD/MM/YYYY`)

All **user-facing** dates in this product use UK format **`DD/MM/YYYY`** (`dd/MM/yyyy` in date-fns). No US, ISO-looking display, or locale-long formats for full dates.

## Required helpers

Prefer shared helpers from `@/utils/date-format`:

```ts
import { formatDateUK, formatDateTimeUK, formatDateISO, UK_DATE_FORMAT } from "@/utils/date-format"

formatDateUK(value)        // → "23/11/2026"
formatDateTimeUK(value)    // → "23/11/2026 14:30"
format(date, UK_DATE_FORMAT) // when you already have a Date
```

## Allowed

| Use | Format |
|---|---|
| Tables, labels, exports (CSV/PDF cells), pickers display | `dd/MM/yyyy` |
| Date + time shown to users | `dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm` |
| `<input type="date">`, API payloads, storage keys | `yyyy-MM-dd` via `formatDateISO` |
| Time-only / relative ("3 hours ago") | OK |
| Calendar chrome (day number, "November 2026" header) | OK |

## Forbidden for display

```ts
// ❌ BAD — never for user-visible full dates
format(date, "MMM dd, yyyy")
format(date, "MMM d, yyyy")
format(date, "dd MMM yyyy")
format(date, "MM-dd-yyyy")
format(date, "yyyy-MM-dd") // display only — OK for inputs/API
format(date, "PPP")
toLocaleDateString()                 // browser-dependent
toLocaleDateString("en-US", { ... })
```

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
formatDateUK(date)
format(date, "dd/MM/yyyy")
toLocaleDateString("en-GB", { day: "2-digit", month: "2-digit", year: "numeric" })
```

## Rule of thumb

If a human reads it as a full date, it must look like **`23/11/2026`**. Nothing else.
